{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating action commits from perception states. The specification enforces always-turn-right recovery, disables forward motion when any obstacle is detected, and ensures quick return to forward progress after recovery. Only move_forward and rotate_clockwise are used as controllable actions, and all obstacle events force right-turn recovery. The design is deterministic, safe, and maximizes exploration progress.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception (clear/obstacle) from action commit states in the plant to model open-loop motion pulses and sensor updates.",
    "Specification automaton disables move_forward in any obstacle state, enables rotate_clockwise as the only recovery, and returns to forward progress as soon as path_clear is observed."
  ],
